 "comments": [
  {
   "address": 1031,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Loads the next level's two files and starts them. Calls the prompt at $0625, then the file loader at $0436 with the file-name pointer for level number $0435, repeats while the error flag $0624 is set, then increments the level number and jumps to the level's entry at $0A20."
  },
  {
   "address": 1077,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Number of the next level to load, 0 to 5, read by the loader loop at $0407 and the prompt at $0625."
  },
  {
   "address": 1078,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stores the file-name pointer from A (low) and Y (high) at $04BE and $04BF, then runs the fast loader at $0493."
  },
  {
   "address": 1087,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Low bytes of the six per-level file-name pointers, indexed by $0435."
  },
  {
   "address": 1093,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "High bytes of the six per-level file-name pointers, indexed by $0435."
  },
  {
   "address": 1548,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "\"DISC ERROR\", shown by the loader when a load fails."
  },
  {
   "address": 1572,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Set when a load fails; makes $0625 show the disk prompt again and $0407 retry the load."
  },
  {
   "address": 1573,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Screen shown between levels. Banks the KERNAL in ($01=$37), sets a text screen at $0400, and prints either the disk-side prompt (before level 1, before level 4, and after an error) or the next-level prompt, then waits for fire on joystick port 2 ($DC00)."
  },
  {
   "address": 1713,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "\"INSERT DISK SIDE #1, THEN PRESS FIRE\"; the side digit is patched to 1 or 2 by $067F before printing."
  },
  {
   "address": 1754,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "\"PRESS FIRE TO LOAD NEXT LEVEL\", shown before levels 2, 3, 5 and 6."
  },
  {
   "address": 45256,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Silences the sound chip: clears the resonance and filter routing at $D417, sets volume 15 at $D418, and zeroes all 21 voice registers $D400-$D414 together with the driver's shadow table at $B02F."
  }
 ]
